  "interpretation": "Overlapping direct paints intersect the image boundary per draw (right-edge alpha192). An enclosing opacity group paints internally and intersects the boundary at restoration (right-edge alpha93 at opacity.73). Both retain corner coverage and shader/packed rounding. A terminal image-alpha multiplication cannot represent both. The existing clip-path machinery reproduces both targets exactly on both platforms.",
  "nextAcceptance": [
    "Preserve the source image boundary independently of logical sizing, authored viewBox and output pixel dimensions.",
    "Keep uniform output scaling and all current text/native targets unchanged.",
    "Consolidate clip-state save/restore before extending its representation. Preserve allocation enclosures while clearing coverage for isolated sources.",
    "Use existing per-draw and group-restore clip behavior; do not add a final pixel correction or a new clip framework.",
    "Avoid allocating a full-surface tape solely for a thin rectangular fringe. Keep per-bitmap border coverage separate from canvas-owned pixels.",
    "Qualify mask/filter source isolation, binary and AA clips, overlapping paints, group restoration, memory refusal/cancellation/cleanup and retry.",
    "Recheck all204 hosted originals without retaining their source collection; run milestone native/runtime/package qualification before root promotion."
  ],
